Hello,

Reporting a reproducible hang on resume from hibernation (S4). On wake, the
kernel logs "The DSDT has been corrupted or replaced", which cascades into
dozens of aborted ACPI methods and finally a runaway ACPI_MTX_Namespace
mutex-acquisition error loop that pins the CPU (259,143 repeats logged in
~80 seconds) until the machine is hard power-cycled. No kernel panic/oops
is logged =E2=80=94 it just spins in the ACPI error loop and journald stops
accepting new lines.

Hardware
--------
Vendor: LENOVO
Product: 83JT / Yoga 7 2-in-1 16ILL10
Board: LNVNB161216, version SDK0T76576 WIN
BIOS: QPCN21WW, dated 2026-01-06 (Insyde)
EC firmware: 1.21
CPU: Intel Core Ultra 7 258V (Lunar Lake)

Kernel
------
Linux 7.0.9-arch2-1 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 22 May 2026 19:25:09 +0000
x86_64
ACPICA version referenced in the error strings: 20251212

How to reproduce
-----------------
1. `systemctl hibernate` (or let systemd-logind's suspend-then-hibernate
lid policy trigger it after the configured delay).
2. Wake the machine (open the lid / power button).
3. Kernel logs "ACPI: PM: Waking up from system sleep state S4",
immediately followed by the DSDT-corrupted error, then a wall of
aborted-method errors, then the machine locks up within roughly 30-90
seconds as the ACPI_MTX_Namespace error loop consumes the CPU.

This is not a one-off: a milder, non-fatal instance of the same
ACPI_MTX_Namespace error (8 lines, machine recovered) was logged two weeks
earlier on this same machine, also around a sleep transition. This time it
did not recover.

dmesg excerpt (resume sequence through first errors)
-----------------------------------------------------
ACPI: PM: Preparing to enter system sleep state S4
...
PM: hibernation: Normal pages needed: 2691139 + 1024, available pages:
5568761
ACPI: PM: Hardware changed while hibernated, success doubtful!
ACPI: PM: Restoring platform NVS memory
ACPI: EC: EC started
...
ACPI: PM: Waking up from system sleep state S4
ACPI BIOS Error (bug): The DSDT has been corrupted or replaced - old, new
headers below (20251212/tbutils-80)
ACPI: DSDT 0x0000000000000000 02AA0C (v02 INSYDE LNL 00000002 ACPI 00040000=
)
ACPI: pT0P 0x0000000000000000 50505445 (v69 T0PRTP PRpT0IPT 70504950 T0EP
50455054)
ACPI Error: Please send DMI info to linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org
If system does not work as expected, please boot with acpi=3Dcopy_dsdt
(20251212/tbutils-87)
ACPI Error: Aborting method \_WAK due to previous error (AE_AML_NO_OPERAND)
(20251212/hwesleep-47)
ACPI BIOS Error (bug): Could not resolve symbol [^MC.PM1H], AE_NOT_FOUND
(20251212/psargs-332)
[... further aborted methods: \ADBG, \_SB.PC00.RP02-RP05 power resource
_STA/_ON, \_TZ.FN00-FN04._STA thermal zones, \_SB.PC00.LPCB.Q_EC.BAT0._STA,
\_SB.PC00.LPCB.Q_EC.ADP1._PSR (AC adapter state),
\_SB.PC00.LPCB.Q_EC.LID0._LID, \_SB.PC00.LPCB.Q_EC.VPC0.DYTC,
\_SB.UBTC._DSM (USB-C), acpi-fan PNP0C0B:00-04 all fail to restore power
state with -19 ...]
ACPI Error: Mutex [ACPI_MTX_Namespace] already acquired by this thread
[425663424] (20251212/utmutex-214)
[repeats 259,143 times over ~80 seconds, then the machine stops responding]

Notably, "ACPI: PM: Hardware changed while hibernated, success doubtful!"
is logged just before the wake completes =E2=80=94 suggesting the EC/firmwa=
re is
not presenting the same platform state (and apparently a
different/regenerated DSDT) across the S4 cycle on this machine.

Additional notes
-----------------
I believe this is the same class of issue described anecdotally on the Arch
Linux forums ("Lunar Lake Laptop Issues Collection Thread"), where
hibernation is reported to randomly lock up Lunar Lake machines on wake. I
have not yet tried acpi=3Dcopy_dsdt as suggested by the kernel's own error
message; happy to test that on request.

Let me know what additional information would help (full dmesg, acpidump -o
output, DSDT disassembly, etc.).

Thanks,
David
